2. Shared glass-card visual language
All three panels use the same overall glassmorphism design language, but their internal transparency and tinting differ slightly.

The panels should look like semi-transparent, blue-tinted glass surfaces floating above the interface.

They are not opaque blue rectangles.

Their visual characteristics are:
- Large rounded corners.
- Semi-transparent blue and teal surfaces.
- Stronger cyan illumination around the outside perimeter.
- A thin, luminous border.
- A subtle brighter upper-edge reflection.
- A darker blue-teal interior tint.
- Soft shadows underneath.
- A frosted appearance.
- Visible underlying scenery through the glass.
- Slightly brighter corners and edge reflections.
Shared CSS foundation
.dashboard-glass {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;

    border: 1px solid rgba(107, 225, 255, 0.76);

    border-radius: 38px;

    background:
        linear-gradient(
            145deg,
            rgba(35, 143, 199, 0.48) 0%,
            rgba(13, 86, 133, 0.57) 42%,
            rgba(5, 65, 92, 0.67) 100%
        );

    backdrop-filter:
        blur(19px)
        saturate(145%);

    -webkit-backdrop-filter:
        blur(19px)
        saturate(145%);

    box-shadow:
        0 8px 26px rgba(0, 35, 65, 0.20),
        0 0 17px rgba(0, 184, 255, 0.15),
        0 0 32px rgba(0, 205, 222, 0.10),
        inset 0 1px 2px rgba(255,255,255,0.35),
        inset 0 -2px 6px rgba(0, 220, 232, 0.15);
}


The values above are starting implementation values; each panel needs its own tint adjustment to match the reference.
Shared upper-edge reflection
The panels have a faint light-blue reflection running along the upper edge.
.dashboard-glass::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;

    border-radius: inherit;
    pointer-events: none;

    background:
        linear-gradient(
            180deg,
            rgba(191, 245, 255, 0.19) 0%,
            rgba(145, 222, 255, 0.08) 13%,
            transparent 38%
        );

    z-index: 0;
}


Important layering rule
Every panel's decorative overlays must sit behind its actual content.
.dashboard-glass > * {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}


Do not let the reflection overlays cover text, icons, graphs, or buttons.

