5.3 Main line
The chart contains a single continuous upward-trending turquoise line.

It starts relatively low on the left.

It rises through several data points, experiences a small plateau, climbs to a higher level, reaches its highest point toward the right, and then fluctuates slightly.

The line is:
- Bright turquoise.
- Approximately 2–3 px thick.
- Smoothly curved.
- Slightly glowing.
- No sharp angular corners.
Use an SVG path with smooth Bézier curves.
Data points
The line has approximately ten visible data points.

Most are small white circular markers.

Each marker is around 9–11 px in diameter.

The points have:
- White fill.
- Slight cyan outer glow.
- No prominent dark outline.
Area fill
Under the line is a translucent cyan-turquoise filled area.

It fades gradually toward the bottom.
.chart-area {
    fill: url(#chartAreaGradient);
}

.chart-line {
    fill: none;

    stroke: #00DCCB;

    stroke-width: 2.5;

    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;

    filter:
        drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgba(0,235,225,0.65));
}


The area gradient should fade from approximately 30% opacity at the top to transparent at the bottom.
